---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
---

<Legal
  title="Cookie policy | DALSAT"
  description="What cookies dalsats.com uses, what they are for, and how to accept, reject or delete them."
  currentPath="/cookies"
  heading="Cookie policy"
  updated="2 September 2026"
  idioma="en"
>
  <div>
    <h2>1. What a cookie is</h2>
    <p>
      A small file a website stores in your browser. It lets the site remember things — for instance,
      whether you have already answered the cookie notice — and in some cases count visits.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>2. What we use</h2>
    <p>
      Very little. One technical cookie to remember your decision and, only if you accept it, Vercel's
      analytics so we know how many people come in and which pages they look at.
    </p>
    <div class="tabla-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>What for</th>
            <th>How long</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>dalsat-consentimiento-cookies</td>
            <td>Technical, always on</td>
            <td>Remembering whether you accepted or rejected, so we do not ask you again</td>
            <td>Until you clear your browser data</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Vercel Analytics</td>
            <td>Analytics, only if you accept</td>
            <td>Counting visits and page views in aggregate, without identifying you</td>
            <td>Aggregate data, no personal profile</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The technical cookie is held in your browser's local storage and never leaves your device. The
      analytics are not loaded until you press "Accept": if you reject, or close without deciding, the
      script is not even downloaded.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>3. First-party and third-party</h2>
    <p>
      The technical one is ours. The analytics belong to Vercel Inc., which hosts the site. We use no
      advertising cookies, no social media cookies and no cross-site tracking.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>4. How to change your mind</h2>
    <p>
      Clear the site data in your browser and the notice will appear again next time you visit, with
      both options. Your browser settings also let you block or delete cookies from any site. If you
      block the technical ones, something may stop working as it should.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>5. More information</h2>
    <p>
      What we do with the data you give us is in the
      <a href="/en/politica-privacidad">privacy policy</a>, and the terms of use of the site are in the
      <a href="/en/aviso-legal">legal notice</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Legal>
